Greetings all,

My apologies if this has been asked previously (a cursory search turned up nothing), but can proportional response data be reliably modeled in occu or colext? I've attempted this without obvious errors, but I don't have enough "under-the-hood" knowledge.

This kind of response is common in a standard glm with binomial error, but I imagine is unlikely when data is collected with occupancy modeling in mind.

Let's take an example: say multiple 10-minute detection/non-detection surveys within a period of closure were divided into subunits. Years later, the (summarized) data provided to the analyst was proportional (e.g. percent of 1-minute periods with detections). Of course the modeler could convert these proportions to a binary response (0 vs. >0), but it would *seem* more information would be contained in the proportional data.

Thanks, as always!

Giancarlo

